  "provenance": "One person-sized object seen ahead at about 55-57 m in doubleT_obstacle, frames 0-104. The reviewer authored the box by hand at frame 0 and re-anchored it at frames 28 and 47; frames 1-24, 29-46 and 48-104 were filled frame by frame by translation-only registration of the box's own returns against each later cloud (nearest neighbour, 0.60 -> 0.12 m, trimmed mean, constant-velocity prediction), and the reviewer then widened the boxes at frames 25-27 by hand. Every written frame holds 73-132 of the object's returns, with the return centroid within 0.15 m of the box centre, so the box follows the object and not a tunnel surface. Measured with the project's own reference contour on the labelled returns, the object starts outside the contour (frames 0-6), is inside over frames 7-68 (100% of returns over 28-60, reaching 0.1 m from the estimated centre line) and is outside again from frame 70, ending 1.2-1.4 m beyond the 1.44-1.46 m half-width for its height; the exit frame lies inside the centre-line 1-sigma of 0.19-0.39 m, frames 78 and later do not. No frame is exhaustive: this records where one object is, not that the frames contain nothing else. The box is a full-person volume, not the support of returns, and its identity as a person is the reviewer's judgement, not a measurement. Frame 105 is present with no box: the reviewer's explicit marker that the object is not there. An empty, non-exhaustive frame scores nothing.",
